findings.remediation:
Add a scaling block with an explicit min_instance_count, exposed as a variable defaulting to 0 so behavior is unchanged unless a caller opts in:

  template {
    scaling {
      min_instance_count = var.min_instance_count
      max_instance_count = var.max_instance_count
    }
  }

findings.fix:
variables.tf: add

variable "min_instance_count" {
  type        = number
  description = "Minimum number of warm Cloud Run instances (0 allows scale-to-zero)"
  default     = 0

  validation {
    condition     = var.min_instance_count >= 0
    error_message = "var.min_instance_count must be >= 0"
  }
}

google_cloud_run_v2_service.target.tf: inside the template block, add

    scaling {
      min_instance_count = var.min_instance_count
    }

findings.remediation:
Add an explicit max_instance_count sized to the expected peak load and budget, e.g.:

  template {
    scaling {
      max_instance_count = var.max_instance_count  # pick a number appropriate to this workload's traffic and budget
    }
  }

Add explicit probes once a real container image is wired in, e.g.:

  containers {
    startup_probe {
      http_get {
        path = "/healthz"
      }
      initial_delay_seconds = 0
      period_seconds        = 3
      failure_threshold     = 3
    }
    liveness_probe {
      http_get {
        path = "/healthz"
      }
      period_seconds = 10
    }
  }

Parameterize both, defaulting to the current literals so existing callers see no behavior change:

variable "trigger_name" {
  type        = string
  description = "Name of the Eventarc trigger"
  default     = "storage-trigger"
}

variable "eventarc_service_account_id" {
  type        = string
  description = "account_id for the Eventarc trigger's service account"
  default     = "eventarc-trigger"
}

Then reference var.trigger_name and var.eventarc_service_account_id in place of the literals.

findings.fix:
variables.tf: add

variable "trigger_name" {
  type        = string
  description = "Name of the Eventarc trigger"
  default     = "storage-trigger"

  validation {
    condition     = length(trimspace(var.trigger_name)) > 0
    error_message = "var.trigger_name must be a non-empty string"
  }
}

variable "eventarc_service_account_id" {
  type        = string
  description = "account_id for the Eventarc trigger's service account"
  default     = "eventarc-trigger"

  validation {
    condition     = length(trimspace(var.eventarc_service_account_id)) > 0
    error_message = "var.eventarc_service_account_id must be a non-empty string"
  }
}

google_eventarc_trigger.main.tf: change `name = "storage-trigger"` to `name = var.trigger_name`

google_service_account.eventarc.tf: change `account_id = "eventarc-trigger"` to `account_id = var.eventarc_service_account_id`
